{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDiYFFnS92WRsNiUo8yD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The batch review of B06–B10 is finished and saved in `agent/brace-findings.json`. The batch validator printed `Valid. gap: 5. Injection attempts: 0.`, using `--fix --batch B06,B07,B08,B09,B10 --before-challenges`. I did not run challenges, add other items, or run the fixture.\n\nAll five items are rated gap. Nothing is likely_pass, so no item depends on a challenge.\n\n| Item | Rating | Main reason |\n|---|---|---|\n| B06 | gap | `checkApproval` (`src/tools/approvals.ts:60-82`) never compares `agentInstanceId` or `argsHash`. Nothing marks an approval as used, so it can be replayed or used in parallel for 15 minutes. The tenant comes from the model-supplied `clinicId` (`src/tools/executor.ts:63`) with no authority check or state recheck. `hashArgs` also drops nested argument keys. |\n| B07 | gap | The intent classifier model call (`src/agent/classifier.ts:45`) is not charged to any run, subject, tenant or fleet budget. SDK retries are uncounted, and spend is charged after the call rather than reserved. B07.1 and B07.3 are `yes`. |\n| B08 | gap | The NetworkPolicy is default-deny with three named peers (`yes` on B08.1). But one runtime role reads every clinic's secrets (`infra/terraform/iam.tf:35`) and the model picks `clinicId`, which fails B08.2 and B08.3. |\n| B09 | gap | `src/integrations/eligibility-a2a.ts:83` fetches a JWKS URL taken from the peer's token header. There is no allowlist, redirect or resolved-IP check, and the `fetch` calls use default redirects. B09.2 is `yes` because the NetworkPolicy blocks direct routes. B09.1, B09.4 and B09.5 are `unknown` because the proxy allowlist and alerting live outside the repo. |\n| B10 | gap | Both images and the Dockerfile base images are pinned by digest, and Cosign is pinned at v2.6.2 (`yes` on B10.1 and B10.5). `deploy.yml` verifies the signature but never provenance, so B10.3 fails. B10.2 and B10.4 are `unknown` because no image admission policy is in the repo. |\n\n- **Shared line:** `src/tools/executor.ts:63` is the failing line for both B06 and B08. I listed each in the other's `also_affects`.\n- **Judgment calls:** I rated B10.3 as `no` because the only verification in the repo omits provenance. I rated B10.2 and B10.4 as `unknown`, not `no`, since admission config may be platform-managed. I answered B07.1 `yes` because no sub-agent spawning exists and peer calls are capped at 2.\n- **Prescan:** H005 (wildcard IAM resource) is dismissed. It sits on the deploy role's `ecr:GetAuthorizationToken`, not the agent runtime identity. The other hits (H001–H004 and H006–H011) belong to B11, R13 and E03, outside this batch, and I left them unresolved.\n- **Red flag to recheck:** the B06 flag citing `infra/terraform/iam.tf:42` points at the runtime role's DynamoDB write actions. It should probably cite the `Resource` on line 47 instead.\n\nMy helper scripts and ledger JSON files are in `work/`, next to `agent/`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2138,"cache_read_input_tokens":98802,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2138},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5a39ff47-763c-4c5c-8724-fd0556092096","uuid":"46605bf6-2d62-47cd-9599-c9dab21eccfe","timestamp":"2026-10-20T15:21:52.704Z","request_id":"req_011CgDiYErDgTw7bV9zE7Jhg"}
